Fungal skin’s response to illumination is manifested in the raising of the baseline potential, as illustrated in the exemplar recordings in Fig. 2c. In contrast to mechanical stimulation response the response-to-illumination spike does not subside but the electrical potential stays raised till illumination is switched off. An average amplitude of the response is 0.61 mV (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
